# the argument of hume-motivation.md as claude-opus-5-5 read it: check that it says what the text says
# Hume's argument that morals are not drawn from reason.
# The step from the two premises to the conclusion relies on an unstated link:
# whatever is derived from reason alone can have no power that reason lacks.
atom	morals_influence	morals have an influence on the actions and affections (excite passions, produce or prevent actions)
atom	reason_influences	reason alone has an influence on the actions and affections
atom	morals_from_reason	morals (the rules of morality) are derived from reason, conclusions of our reason
P1	S2	morals_influence	kind empirical
P2	S3	¬reason_influences
A1	-	morals_from_reason → (morals_influence → reason_influences)
C	S4	¬morals_from_reason	from P1 P2 A1
